{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggEQjeCZM47jRai59GCG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[33, 33, 34]`, so the shares always add up to the total. The leftover grosze go one each to the last people in the list.\n\nI had to change `receipt.py` as well. Its `receipt_lines` already patched the bug by adding the remainder to the last person's share. With `split_cents` fixed, that patch would have charged the extra grosze twice, so I removed it. Because of this I also ran `test_receipt.py` alongside `test_money.py`. Both files pass (6 tests). I didn't run the full suite.\n\n- **Change:** when the remainder is 2 or more, it's now spread one grosz per person instead of all going to the last person. For example, 1001 split three ways is now 3,33 / 3,34 / 3,34 instead of 3,33 / 3,33 / 3,35. Cases with a remainder of 1, like the existing receipt test, come out the same as before.\n- **New test:** I added an uneven-split test to `test_money.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":20182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":558},"output_tokens":334,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ae0c6ca-b105-4075-9dc1-3b5429ee823c","uuid":"89c7eaed-6cac-4eef-82f6-49ff2209fdba","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:28:57.486Z","request_id":"req_011CggEQjNarkC8CddsqJykV"}
